session Second_Order_Viscosity_Analysis = Symmetric_Matrix_Spectra +
  description "
    The complete second-order machinery for comparison proofs between
    viscosity solutions: Rademacher's theorem, Alexandrov's theorem, Jensen's
    lemma for semiconvex functions, the Crandall-Ishii theorem on sums, and
    the doubling-of-variables and soft-penalty toolboxes they exist to
    serve -- and, on top of them, the test-function class and the definition
    of a viscosity sub- and supersolution for an arbitrary second-order
    operator, test class and touching locality.  Built on Symmetric_Matrix_Spectra for the matrix calculus,
    and on Semicontinuous_Analysis for semicontinuity and attainment.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    Semicontinuous_Analysis
  theories
    Convex_Subgradients
    Rademacher
    Moreau_Envelope
    Alexandrov
    Jensen_Lemma
    Sup_Convolution
    Theorem_On_Sums
    Doubling_Of_Variables
    Crandall_Ishii_Sums
    Soft_Penalty
    Test_Functions
    Viscosity_Solutions
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
